{"tool_name":"elixir-a","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"elixir-a","home":"https://github.com/sfernando-BAEN/ELIXIR-A/releases","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Enhanced Ligand Exploration and Interaction Recognition Algorithm (ELIXIR-A). ELIXIR-A, a plugin in VMD, can find similarities in the active site of the receptor under study compared to other receptors.","addition_date":"2022-08-01T12:05:31.034317Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:51:07.525204Z","tool_type":["Plug-in"],"version":["2.1"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:elixir-a","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"sfernando@tamu.edu","name":"Sandun Fernando","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7692-2170","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Haoqi Wang"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Optimisation and refinement","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2425"},{"term":"Virtual screening","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3938"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"ELIXIR-A","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1021/acsomega.1c07144","metadata":{"abstract":"Pharmacophore modeling is an important step in computer-aided drug design for identifying interaction points between the receptor and ligand complex. Pharmacophore-based models can be used for de novo drug design, lead identification, and optimization in virtual screening as well as for multi-target drug design. There is a need to develop a user-friendly interface to filter the pharmacophore points resulting from multiple ligand conformations. Here, we present ELIXIR-A, a Python-based pharmacophore refinement tool, to help refine the pharmacophores between multiple ligands from multiple receptors. Furthermore, the output can be easily used in virtual pharmacophore-based screening platforms, thereby contributing to the development of d